### Is Elon Musk really giving every kid a SpaceX share?
[Elon Musk](https://x.com/elonmusk) stated on social media that he plans to donate stock, and [SpaceX](https://www.spacex.com/) confirmed on November 25, 2026, that it plans to issue one Class A share to every active Trump Account. Musk announced that he will personally match the corporate contribution with one of his own shares. This follows his October 19, 2026 post on X pledging a share to every child in America next year.

### Do I need to claim my child's Trump Account to get the SpaceX share?
No official source states that claiming an account is required to receive the SpaceX share, nor has any source confirmed that claiming makes an account active. You must still claim your child's auto-enrolled account at [trumpaccounts.gov](https://trumpaccounts.gov) or through the official mobile app to unlock family contributions and secure the one-time $1,000 Treasury seed for eligible children. The verification process requires confirming your identity, verifying your relationship to the child, and accepting the account terms.

### What does an active Trump Account mean for the SpaceX share?
Neither the [SpaceX release](https://ir.spacex.com/updates/releases-details/2026/SpaceX-to-Invest-in-the-Next-Generation-of-Americans-2026-r_LYQ5cH94/default.aspx) nor [CNBC](https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/25/spacex-musk-trump-account-stock.html) defines what qualifies an account as active. The White House reported in October 2026 that nearly 70 million accounts had been created, but CNBC noted that it remains unclear how many are considered active. Until SpaceX or federal administrators publish explicit eligibility standards, active status remains unconfirmed.

### When will the SpaceX share arrive in my child's Trump Account?
SpaceX has not announced an official distribution date for its corporate share donation. For his matching personal share, Musk posted on X that the transfer will occur after his lockup period expires in June 2027, as reported by CNBC. While an earlier separate gift of over two million shares from Gwynne Shotwell is expected to arrive in December 2026, no source reports that the corporate SpaceX share will arrive in December.

### Can my child sell the SpaceX share?
Beneficiaries generally cannot sell donated shares right away, according to CNBC citing Treasury rules. Those rules state that stock gifts cannot be sold until the earlier of five years or the end of the calendar year in which the beneficiary turns 17. Furthermore, CNBC reported that families cannot refuse stock gifts deposited into an account.

### Is the 'claim your free SpaceX share' message I got a scam?
Yes, any unsolicited message directing you to claim a SpaceX share through an external link is an unauthorized scam. Official program emails originate exclusively from no-reply@TrumpAccounts.Treasury.gov, and genuine account actions occur only on trumpaccounts.gov or within the official Treasury app. Never pay a fee, send cryptocurrency, or enter your child's Social Security number on an unverified website, and you can report suspicious communications to Treasury at 1-866-USA-4547.